=== BRANCH C: tiling / Walsh decomposition of D(T) (HYP-2335, BLUE conjecture) ===
Bit convention: bit=1 iff arc x->y (explorer stores complement; grid-sym unaffected).
Relabeling: u_i -> n+i, v_j -> n+1-j  (path position t gets label 2n-t).

--- S2: exhaustive verification of block transform + BLUE verdict ---
n=3: tilings=2  BLUE(D)=0/2  block-formula exact=2/2  defect==cross-offtwin=2/2  weight law 2|x|+(n-1)+C(n,2)=2/2  [|defect| = n(n-1) = 6 tiles = 3 sigma-pairs of 4]
n=4: tilings=8  BLUE(D)=0/8  block-formula exact=8/8  defect==cross-offtwin=8/8  weight law 2|x|+(n-1)+C(n,2)=8/8  [|defect| = n(n-1) = 12 tiles = 6 sigma-pairs of 9]
n=5: tilings=64  BLUE(D)=0/64  block-formula exact=64/64  defect==cross-offtwin=64/64  weight law 2|x|+(n-1)+C(n,2)=64/64  [|defect| = n(n-1) = 20 tiles = 10 sigma-pairs of 16]
n=6: tilings=1024  BLUE(D)=0/1024  block-formula exact=1024/1024  defect==cross-offtwin=1024/1024  weight law 2|x|+(n-1)+C(n,2)=1024/1024  [|defect| = n(n-1) = 30 tiles = 15 sigma-pairs of 25]

--- S2b: same over ALL labeled tournaments (insertion-path frame), n=3..5 ---
n=3: labeled=8  BLUE(D)=0/8  formula=8/8  defect-const=8/8
n=4: labeled=64  BLUE(D)=0/64  formula=64/64  defect-const=64/64
n=5: labeled=1024  BLUE(D)=0/1024  formula=1024/1024  defect-const=1024/1024

--- S3: sigma-image identification ---
n=3: sigma(t)=t^c (const coset) 2/2;  sigma(t) = tiling(swap-relabeled D(T)^op) 2/2;  sigma(t) != t always (so sigma-image never a D-image) 2/2
n=4: sigma(t)=t^c (const coset) 8/8;  sigma(t) = tiling(swap-relabeled D(T)^op) 8/8;  sigma(t) != t always (so sigma-image never a D-image) 8/8
n=5: sigma(t)=t^c (const coset) 64/64;  sigma(t) = tiling(swap-relabeled D(T)^op) 64/64;  sigma(t) != t always (so sigma-image never a D-image) 64/64
sigma(t(D(T))) IS the canonical tiling of D(T)^op (copy-swap relabeled = path-reversal frame).

--- S4: Walsh schema at tile level, example n=4 (frame size 8) ---
Region map (rows X=8..2, cols Y=1..7; 1/0 = tile bit, P = base path, . = none):
   regions: X,Y in 5..8 -> COPY-1 = x ; X,Y in 1..4 -> COPY-2 = sigma_4(x) ;
            X in 5..8, Y in 1..4 -> CROSS = A(T) full arc matrix, anti-diag X+Y=9 twins=1
     Y=1 Y=2 Y=3 Y=4 Y=5 Y=6 Y=7
X=8:   1   1   1   1   1   1   P
X=7:   0   1   1   0   0   P   .
X=6:   0   0   1   1   P   .   .
X=5:   0   1   0   P   .   .   .
X=4:   1   0   P   .   .   .   .
X=3:   1   P   .   .   .   .   .
X=2:   P   .   .   .   .   .   .
x(T) = [1, 0, 1] (tiles A=(4,1),B=(3,1),C=(4,2));  A(T) arcs include base path 4->3->2->1
Tile-level Walsh schema [[H,H],[H,-H]] reading:
  +copy 1: copy-1 block = x ;  +copy 2: copy-2 block = sigma(x) (grid transpose, NO negation);
  cross block = +copy 3 and -copy 4 INTERLEAVED: pair {i,j} appears as A[i][j] AND A[j][i]=NOT A[i][j];
  the all-ones twin anti-diagonal (X+Y=2n+1) is the identity/border (the "+I" of the matrix schema).

--- S5: x -> t(D(x)) is an injective AFFINE-LINEAR map over GF(2) ---
n=3: affine law holds 2/2 (sampled);  GF(2) rank of linear part = 1 (= C(n-1,2) = 1 => injective);  blue-subspace dim at 2n = n(n-1) = 6;  density of D-image in its coset = 2^-5
n=4: affine law holds 8/8 (sampled);  GF(2) rank of linear part = 3 (= C(n-1,2) = 3 => injective);  blue-subspace dim at 2n = n(n-1) = 12;  density of D-image in its coset = 2^-9
n=5: affine law holds 64/64 (sampled);  GF(2) rank of linear part = 6 (= C(n-1,2) = 6 => injective);  blue-subspace dim at 2n = n(n-1) = 20;  density of D-image in its coset = 2^-14

